From c6fbf3469f4be0ab7cc510665425c53ef0fe18b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MR. ARX" <dev@nexeris.dev>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:23:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign video/class page to match reference: breadcrumb +
 Course Content/You may also like sidebar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Two-column layout: player/title/download/resources/description on
  the left, a real sidebar on the right.
- Breadcrumb (Learn > parent board > this board) using the actual
  board hierarchy, 2 levels deep — same reasoning as elsewhere in this
  app (boards can nest arbitrarily but the UI groups by subject).
- Course Content panel reuses the existing PartsList (siblings in this
  board, 'Now playing' indicator) inside a card matching the reference.
- New 'You may also like' panel: real videos pulled from sibling
  boards under the same parent, most recent first.
- Deliberately NOT included: an 'Instructor' name and per-video
  duration, both shown in the reference — neither field exists in the
  schema (videos has no instructor/duration column), and fabricating
  them would show fake information as if it were real data. Durations
  are technically fetchable from Bunny's API per-video but that's an
  extra round-trip per class; happy to wire that up if wanted, or add
  a real instructor column+admin field if you want that to be a thing
  classes actually have.
---
